  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1137 PM CDT TUE SEP 22 2026\n\nAs a cold front slowly moves through the region into Wednesday,\nshower and thunderstorm activity will gradually taper off from\nnorthwest to southeast. A few stronger storms remain possible\nacross the northeast through Wednesday afternoon as the front\nprogresses. A deepening trough will develop to our east Wednesday\nthrough the weekend while a ridge builds to our west. Until the\nridge becomes firmly established, isolated showers may persist\nalong the front in western areas through early Thursday\nafternoon.\n\nFollowing several weeks of above-normal temperatures, a welcome\ntransition to fall-like conditions is expected. Daytime highs\nwill range from the low to mid-80s across much of the area, with\nupper 70s limited to far eastern portions of Central Alabama.\nOvernight lows will drop into the mid-to-upper 50s across\nnorthern sections, with lower-to-middle 60s further south. This\ndry, seasonable regime will persist through the upcoming weekend\nand into early next week, bringing tranquil conditions and little\nto no rain potential across all of Central Alabama.\n\n16",
